Description: Report the screen edge a window drag is at on the IPC event stream
 macOS tiles a window dragged to a screen edge or corner: a half, a quarter, or
 the whole screen from the top edge, with a preview while the pointer rests
 there. niri does not know these zones. This adds two transient event-stream
 events: WindowMoveEdgeChanged { id, edge } while an interactive move enters
 or leaves an edge or corner, and WindowMoveEnded { id, edge } when it ends.
 niri still leaves the window where it was dropped; the Lulo OS window service
 (rmac-mission-control) previews and applies the tile, through the same
 floating-frame actions as Window > Move & Resize.
 .
 See docs/decisions/0029-edge-drag-tiling.md in the rmac repository.
Author: Jacob Samas <samasjacob@icloud.com>
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-20
